+\section{Introduction}
+\label{sec:intro}
+
+% Motivation: corpora are graphs, standard LM training flattens them.
+\todo{Open with the graph-structure-is-ignored motivation (Wikipedia links, Python
+imports, arXiv citations as three concrete edge types).}
+
+% The gap: retrieval/RAG uses links at inference; packing work orders docs but adds
+% no cross-doc attention; GNN/graph-LM work message-passes but doesn't train a
+% decoder-only LM's attention along edges.
+\todo{State the gap precisely against the three neighbouring literatures
+(retrieval-augmented LMs, sequence packing, graph-aware pretraining) --- pull from
+related work once the lit-review returns.}
+
+% Contribution list.
+\paragraph{Contributions.}
+\begin{itemize}
+  \item A pretraining framework that packs documents by graph traversal and grants
+        \emph{link-position-gated} cross-document attention along explicit edges
+        (\Cref{sec:method}).
+  \item Compute-controlled ablations (\concatlink, \concat) that attribute the gain
+        to the linking inductive bias rather than to extra attention FLOPs.
+  \item Evidence across three edge modalities---Wikipedia hyperlinks, code imports,
+        arXiv citations---that cross-document attention beats flat concatenation of
+        the same linked content on benchmarks built to require it, while remaining
+        neutral on single-document benchmarks.
+  \item A density-aware batch scheduler that removes the DDP rank imbalance caused
+        by variable mask sparsity, for a $1.45\times$ mean step speedup.
+  \item An inference/generation loop that resolves generated links against the
+        corpus and injects the target document, mirroring training.
+\end{itemize}
+

diff --git a/paper/sections/02_related_work.tex b/paper/sections/02_related_work.tex
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1234567
--- /dev/null
+++ b/paper/sections/02_related_work.tex
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+\section{Related Work}
+\label{sec:related}
+
+% Organizing principle: every neighbouring line either (a) uses links only at
+% inference/retrieval time, or (b) trains on structure but not as a cross-document
+% attention edge in a decoder-only LM. \method is the intersection nobody occupies.
+% Notes with per-paper detail live in paper/bib/raw/*.md.
+
+\paragraph{Retrieval-augmented language models.}
+A large body of work injects external documents at inference time. RAG
+\citep{lewis2020rag}, Fusion-in-Decoder \citep{izacard2021fid}, Atlas
+\citep{izacard2023atlas}, REPLUG \citep{shi2024replug} and in-context RALM
+\citep{ram2023incontextralm} prepend or fuse retrieved passages as text; REALM
+\citep{guu2020realm} uniquely back-propagates through retrieval during
+pretraining; Self-RAG \citep{asai2024selfrag} trains the model to decide when to
+retrieve. In all of these the linked/retrieved content is selected by learned
+embedding similarity and integrated as text, not by a ground-truth link graph.
+\method instead packs the \emph{actually-linked} documents in-sequence and lets
+attention span them, so cross-document information flow is learned end-to-end
+along known edges rather than bolted on via a separate retriever.
+
+\paragraph{Cached-KV and external-memory attention.}
+The closest inference-time analogues store key/value states rather than text.
+Memorizing Transformers \citep{wu2022memorizing} attach a non-differentiable,
+frozen $k$NN memory of past $(k,v)$ pairs to one attention layer; $k$NN-LM
+\citep{khandelwal2020knnlm} interpolates a frozen LM with a datastore of cached
+hidden states; RETRO \citep{borgeaud2022retro} cross-attends to chunk encodings
+retrieved from a frozen trillion-token store; Unlimiformer \citep{bertsch2023unlimiformer},
+Landmark Attention \citep{mohtashami2023landmark} and the Focused Transformer
+\citep{tworkowski2023focused} all retrieve cached states into attention at
+inference. Google's Mention Memory / TOME \citep{dejong2022tome} and LUMEN
+\citep{dejong2023lumen} precompute a \emph{corpus-wide} memory that is frozen and
+attention-injected without training on it. \method differs on two axes: the
+cached content is keyed by document/node granularity along explicit links, and the
+cross-document attention is a first-class \emph{pretraining} objective, active in
+both training and inference, rather than a frozen store queried only at test time.
+Recent serving-side KV-cache reuse for RAG---Prompt Cache \citep{gim2024promptcache},
+CacheBlend \citep{yao2025cacheblend}, Block-Attention \citep{ma2025blockattention}
+and Cache-Augmented Generation \citep{chan2025cag}---precompute per-document KV and
+splice it into attention; Block-Attention is notable for \emph{fine-tuning} the
+model to a block-structured mask, paralleling our train-and-inference mask, but its
+blocks are a flat set of retrieved passages, not graph-structured links.
+
+\paragraph{Graph-aware and link-aware pretraining.}
+LinkBERT \citep{yasunaga2022linkbert} is the closest antecedent to our core idea:
+it places hyperlinked documents in the same context and adds a document-relation
+objective---genuinely training on links, but as an encoder with MLM, over document
+\emph{pairs}, and with full (not link-gated) attention. Text-attributed-graph
+methods encode structure through GNN message passing rather than an attention edge:
+GraphFormers \citep{yang2021graphformers}, Patton \citep{jin2023patton}, Heterformer
+\citep{jin2023heterformer}, Edgeformers \citep{jin2023edgeformers}, GLEM
+\citep{zhao2023glem} and GNN-LM \citep{meng2022gnnlm}, surveyed by
+\citet{jin2024llmgraphsurvey}; Graphormer \citep{ying2021graphormer} injects graph
+structure as additive attention-score biases over small graphs. Entity-knowledge
+injection (KnowBERT \citep{peters2019knowbert}, ERNIE \citep{zhang2019ernie},
+K-Adapter \citep{wang2021kadapter}, Entities-as-Experts \citep{fevry2020eae}) fuses
+KB entities into token representations. \method keeps a vanilla decoder-only LM and
+moves all graph structure into sequence packing plus a hard block-sparse attention
+mask, targeting autoregressive generation rather than node embeddings.
+
+\paragraph{Sequence packing and document composition.}
+In-Context Pretraining \citep{shi2024incontext} and SPLiCe
+\citep{staniszewski2025structured} pack \emph{related} documents into each training
+sequence---by nearest-neighbour retrieval and a traversal-style ordering---but apply
+standard causal attention with no cross-document mechanism. \citet{zhao2024analysing}
+show cross-document attention over concatenated documents is harmful and advocate
+intra-document boundary masking; best-fit packing \citep{ding2024fewer} optimizes
+document integrity. \method starts from the same block-diagonal isolation of
+\emph{unrelated} documents but selectively \emph{re-enables} cross-document
+attention along explicit link edges---the mechanism these works either omit or
+deliberately mask out.
+
+\paragraph{Long-context and sparse attention.}
+Our masks are made tractable at 32k context by PyTorch FlexAttention
+\citep{flexattention_blog2024,flexattention_paper2024}, which compiles a
+\texttt{mask\_mod} predicate into a block-sparse kernel built on FlashAttention
+\citep{dao2022flashattention,dao2023flashattention2}. Prior sparse-attention
+patterns---Sparse Transformers \citep{child2019sparsetransformers}, Longformer
+\citep{beltagy2020longformer}, BigBird \citep{zaheer2020bigbird}---use fixed
+geometric templates; our sparsity is \emph{data-defined} by the document link
+graph. CoLT5 \citep{ainslie2023colt5} and Ring Attention \citep{liu2023ringattention}
+address the orthogonal conditional-computation and distributed-attention axes.
+
+\paragraph{Repository-level code modeling.}
+DeepSeek-Coder \citep{guo2024deepseekcoder} is the closest code analogue: it
+topologically sorts files by their import graph so dependencies precede dependents,
+then concatenates them---but applies plain causal attention with no edge-keyed
+cross-file attention, exactly the gap \method fills. StarCoder/StarCoder2
+\citep{li2023starcoder,lozhkov2024starcoder2} pack same-repo files with delimiters
+under full attention. A parallel line supplies cross-file context by
+\emph{inference-time} retrieval: RepoCoder \citep{zhang2023repocoder}, CrossCodeEval
+\citep{ding2023crosscodeeval}, CoCoMIC \citep{ding2024cocomic}, RepoFusion
+\citep{shrivastava2023repofusion}, RepoHyper \citep{phan2024repohyper}, RLPG
+\citep{shrivastava2023rlpg} and monitor-guided decoding \citep{agrawal2023monitor}.
+We evaluate on RepoBench \citep{liu2024repobench} over The Stack
+\citep{kocetkov2022stack}, with single-file benchmarks
+\citep{chen2021humaneval,austin2021mbpp,muennighoff2024octopack,lu2021codexglue} as
+controls.
+
+\paragraph{Multi-hop QA and text-attributed-graph corpora.}
+Our headline capability test derives from HotpotQA \citep{yang2018hotpotqa};
+related multi-hop benchmarks include WikiHop \citep{welbl2018wikihop},
+2WikiMultiHopQA \citep{ho2020twowiki}, MuSiQue \citep{trivedi2022musique}, HoVer
+\citep{jiang2020hover}, StrategyQA \citep{geva2021strategyqa} and Bamboogle
+\citep{press2023bamboogle}. Prior graph readers for multi-hop QA build a reasoning
+graph consumed by a GNN at inference \citep{ding2019cognitivegraph,tu2019hde,qiu2019dfgn};
+we instead bake the graph into pretraining attention. Our training corpora are
+themselves text-attributed graphs: Wikipedia hyperlink networks
+\citep{consonni2019wikilinkgraphs,merity2017pointer} and arXiv citation graphs from
+unarXive \citep{saier2020unarxive,saier2023unarxive}, S2ORC \citep{lo2020s2orc} and
+OGB \citep{hu2020ogb}. Citation edges have previously shaped document \emph{embeddings}
+(SPECTER \citep{cohan2020specter}, SciNCL \citep{ostendorff2022scincl}, SciBERT
+\citep{beltagy2019scibert}); we instead condition a generative LM on them via
+cross-document attention. Single-document commonsense benchmarks
+\citep{zellers2019hellaswag,clark2018arc,bisk2020piqa,sakaguchi2020winogrande,mihaylov2018openbookqa,clark2019boolq}
+serve as controls where cross-document attention should---and does---have no effect.
+

